    {
      "_comment": "PACE sweep, 0.5 s per step. 0.5 is exactly neutral (x1); 0.0 is the slowest end, 1.0 the fastest. The whole range is covered, and it returns to neutral so the ear has the same reference at both ends of the file. duration_s is 61, not 60: the render loop runs i < duration_s * sample_rate, so the last t it reaches at 60 s would be 59.99998 and the closing return to neutral at t = 60.0 would never fire. The extra second also lets that return be heard."
    },
